<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:35:31 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Amid uncertainty over EU aid, Vitalii Kim insists Ukraine has no choice but to fight for motherland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261028-amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Vitalii Kim, Minister for Veterans Affairs of Ukraine. “If Europe will not support us, we also will fight because it's our motherland,” says Kim, insisting that Ukraine's determination to resist Russian aggression will endure regardless of the outcome of negotiations over European financial assistance. Yet behind this assertion of national resolve lies a more complex reality: a country confronting not only the immediate pressures of war, but also its mounting psychological, social and institutional consequences.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89bfec5e-d304-11f1-8b0d-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-183320-184320-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89bfec5e-d304-11f1-8b0d-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-183320-184320-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8c8f4e4-d309-11f1-9eaa-9f7beea5bd43</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:57:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Amid uncertainty over EU aid, Vitalii Kim insists Ukraine has no choice but to fight for motherland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/amid-uncertainty-over-eu-aid-vitalii-kim-insists-ukraine-has-no-choice-but-to-fight-for-motherland</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Vitalii Kim, Minister for Veterans Affairs of Ukraine. “If Europe will not support us, we also will fight because it's our motherland,” says Kim, insisting that Ukraine's determination to resist Russian aggression will endure regardless of the outcome of negotiations over European financial assistance. Yet behind this assertion of national resolve lies a more complex reality: a country confronting not only the immediate pressures of war, but also its mounting psychological, social and institutional consequences.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89bfec5e-d304-11f1-8b0d-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-183320-184320-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89bfec5e-d304-11f1-8b0d-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-183320-184320-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">90159cd4-d304-11f1-bc4e-6734684b1e6c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:54:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain high-speed train crash kills 68, injures over 100</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spain-high-speed-train-crash-kills-68-injures-over-100</link><description>
A high-speed train collision south of Madrid killed 68 people and injured scores more on Wednesday, with the toll likely to rise, authorities said, in one of Europe's deadliest such disasters this century. The second such accident to strike Spain this year will raise fresh questions about the country's rail safety, with the transport minister speaking of an "error" and "inexplicable circumstances" that led to the collision. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Urda, south of Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9520b7d6-d304-11f1-bd08-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-200141-200812-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9520b7d6-d304-11f1-bd08-811458fcf026/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-200141-200812-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b04af72-d304-11f1-86b8-ff36709a27e3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:32:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Racist attack in Trappes deeply scars local community</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-france-racist-attack-in-trappes-deeply-scars-local-community</link><description>
It has been five days since a gunman opened fire in the Paris suburb of Trappes in a racist attack that left one person dead and five others injured. Over the weekend, hundreds of people marched through the town to pay tribute to the 26-year-old victim, Bossio Wangi, and show solidarity with his family. The attack has left a deep mark on the local community, and mediators have been mobilised to provide support. Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a476116e-d1f5-11f1-8114-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T185301Z-1414144200-RC26BOAZJ25N-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-SECURITY-SHOOTING-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a476116e-d1f5-11f1-8114-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T185301Z-1414144200-RC26BOAZJ25N-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-SECURITY-SHOOTING-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f57cde30-d2ea-11f1-a945-c521a8b0ffb6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:53:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>At least 64 dead in Spain’s high-speed train crash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-at-least-64-dead-in-spain-s-high-speed-train-crash</link><description>
At least 64 people died when two Spanish ​high-speed trains collided on Wednesday, with rescue workers scouring the wreckage for more bodies after Spain's second deadly rail accident this year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae847f2a-d2df-11f1-a8ff-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/minispain.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae847f2a-d2df-11f1-a8ff-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/minispain.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdab69c2-d2df-11f1-8527-05fba03596ab</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:37:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Spanish Transport Minister gives press conference on train crash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-replay-spanish-transport-minister-gives-press-conference-on-train-crash</link><description>
A high-speed train collision south of Madrid killed 64 people and injured scores more on Wednesday (October 28), with the toll likely to rise, authorities said in one of Europe's deadliest such disasters this century. Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente gave some details in a press conference.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/11ee45dc-d2db-11f1-a7df-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-144955-150257-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/11ee45dc-d2db-11f1-a7df-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-144955-150257-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">170370ec-d2db-11f1-9f13-1fc167e9264e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:43:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain: Dozens killed after one high-speed train slams into another</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-dozens-killed-after-one-high-speed-train-slams-into-another</link><description>
Spain suffered its second deadly high-speed train accident this year when one train on Wednesday, October 28, slammed into another that had stopped on the tracks, with the impact shredding cars and killing at least 64 people. The accident comes with memories still fresh of another crash between high-speed trains in southern Spain in January. France 24's correspondent in Madrid Sarah Morris gives us the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab664304-d2db-11f1-8d4a-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-150308-150809-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ab664304-d2db-11f1-8d4a-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-150308-150809-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b099b2c0-d2db-11f1-8fcc-7fa17db54773</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:34:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain: At least 64 dead in high-speed train crash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-64-dead-in-high-speed-train-crash</link><description>
In Spain, a high-speed train slammed into the rear of another train that had stopped, derailing two cars and killing at least 64 people on Wednesday, October 28. The central government’s office for Castilla La Mancha confirmed the death toll had risen. It is the second major train accident in Spain this year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9cd31ca-d2da-11f1-91d1-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-98244578.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9cd31ca-d2da-11f1-91d1-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-98244578.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f7e2db2-d2d8-11f1-a69a-bd02d4400efd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:33:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine: Melania Trump-brokered local ceasefire holds for second day</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-melania-trump-brokered-local-ceasefire-holds-for-second-day</link><description>
There ​have been ​no breaches of the US-brokered local ceasefire ​around ‌the ⁠Russian-occupied town of Oleshky ‌in southern Ukraine during its first 30 hours, ​Ukraine's human rights ‌ombudsman Dmytro Lubinets said on ‌Wednesday. A ceasefire has ​been agreed until November 1 to ​allow residents of ​the frontline ​town – who had ​been unable to leave amid near-uninhabitable conditions – to evacuate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f06a6ef4-d2cb-11f1-9aeb-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-38.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f06a6ef4-d2cb-11f1-9aeb-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-38.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3498e13c-d2cc-11f1-83bd-33d76fee02c7</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:42:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine: Ceasefire holds for its first 30 hours in occupied Oleshky</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-ceasefire-holds-for-its-first-30-hours-in-occupied-oleshky</link><description>
A local ceasefire in the Russian-occupied southern Ukrainian city of Oleshky held through its first day and night, despite continued fighting between Moscow and Kyiv elsewhere. The truce, which began on Tuesday in the devastated city, is expected to remain in place until Sunday. Emerald Maxwell reports. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/34c0ad2c-d2b6-11f1-b05f-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-101958-102153-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/34c0ad2c-d2b6-11f1-b05f-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-101958-102153-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">39ae8dd6-d2b6-11f1-a18b-81f676a00804</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:46:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain: At least 10 dead in crash between 2 high-speed trains</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-10-dead-in-crash-between-2-high-speed-trains</link><description>
At least ten people have died in a crash between two trains in central Spain. The crash occurred Wednesday morning  in the province of Toledo. Rail service is suspended between Madrid, Ciudad Real and Andalusia.
 
France 24's correspondent in Madrid Sarah Morris reports the latest. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5208860-d2b3-11f1-9e26-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-101223-101424-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5208860-d2b3-11f1-9e26-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-101223-101424-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">faaffa40-d2b3-11f1-b3d1-439f4bfd1d91</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:11:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spain to observe three days of mourning after scores killed in high-speed train collision</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-two-high-speed-trains-collide-in-southern-spain-rail-operator-says</link><description>
At least 68 people were killed Wednesday after two high-speed trains collided in Spain's central Toledo province, regional authorities confirmed, with high-speed rail services between Madrid and Andalusia suspended. It is Spain's second deadly train crash in less than a year. Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said the country would observe three days of mourning. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b95a0fb6-d2c9-11f1-93fc-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26301441408849.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b95a0fb6-d2c9-11f1-93fc-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26301441408849.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ec4e8c2-d2ad-11f1-a4ba-7f054befa3c0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:00:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b95a0fb6-d2c9-11f1-93fc-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26301441408849.jpg">© Manu Fernandez, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How student assemblies brought down the Serbian government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-how-student-assemblies-brought-down-the-serbian-government</link><description>
A list of academics, engineers, artists and activists chosen by Serbia’s student assemblies defeated long-ruling president Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing Serbian Progressive Party Sunday. The shock victory comes after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests – and may serve as a model for other movements hoping to turn street demonstrations into concrete political change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4370c334-d225-11f1-9cd7-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T200342Z-473553852-RC26BOAEJNFQ-RTRMADP-3-SERBIA-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4370c334-d225-11f1-9cd7-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T200342Z-473553852-RC26BOAEJNFQ-RTRMADP-3-SERBIA-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58ef0ee2-d224-11f1-aae6-b7e084e46075</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:58:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4370c334-d225-11f1-9cd7-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T200342Z-473553852-RC26BOAEJNFQ-RTRMADP-3-SERBIA-ELECTION.jpg">© Marko Djurica, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Lawmakers hold a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi, victim of racist attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-lawmakers-hold-a-minute-of-silence-for-pengo-bossio-wangi-victim-of-racist-attack-1</link><description>
French lawmakers held a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi. The victim of a racist attack died in a shooting last week, while at least five other people were wounded, including a 12-years-old girl. FRANCE 24’s Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d26e3818-d226-11f1-a4c7-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3b57773c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d26e3818-d226-11f1-a4c7-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3b57773c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fa737d4c-d225-11f1-888e-9500dea4febf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:08:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France's Senate takes on the 'rioters pay' bill after protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-s-senate-takes-on-the-rioters-pay-bill-after-protests</link><description>
If the French Senate passes this bill, rioters will have to pay for the damage caused during the recent unrest across the country. This "casseurs-payeurs" bill comes in the wake of nationwide violence. This draft law now has an explosive add-on aimed at social media. Senators will vote on whether the government can block platforms that are too slow to act on authorities' reports of dangerous content. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e52261dc-d1fe-11f1-b43c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1c3031f6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e52261dc-d1fe-11f1-b43c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1c3031f6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8b96ed1e-d1fd-11f1-b4b7-85fc3689f01c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:13:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Localised Russia-Ukraine ceasefire starts in Ukrainian town facing starvation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-localised-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-starts-ukrainian-town-facing-starvation</link><description>
A localised ceasefire between Ukraine and Russia took effect early Tuesday (October 27) ahead of a humanitarian mission led by US first lady Melania Trump, as missile attacks resumed in Kyiv. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv, Emmanuelle Chaze, has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eda218e8-d1a4-11f1-9062-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/37d1dc6b018faa3403f2a1f253bd0bc47e1a1ebe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eda218e8-d1a4-11f1-9062-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/37d1dc6b018faa3403f2a1f253bd0bc47e1a1ebe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">360e782c-d1fc-11f1-9903-8f0754652aee</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:34:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ballon d’Or winner Harry Kane delivers emotional acceptance speech</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ballon-d-or-winner-harry-kane-delivers-emotional-acceptance-speech</link><description>
Harry Kane became the first Englishman in 25 years to win the Ballon d’Or on Monday. Kane scored 73 goals for club and country last campaign and smashed scoring records at the World Cup, where he captained England to a third-place finish.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88b0c438-d1ff-11f1-8eeb-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/minikane.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88b0c438-d1ff-11f1-8eeb-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/minikane.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac880998-d1ff-11f1-b96e-f143e24026c3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:20:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French protests: Student union leaders vow to keep mobilising</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-french-protests-student-union-leaders-vow-to-keep-mobilising</link><description>
In France, after weeks of student unrest, the government announced new school measures. Student union leaders said it's a first step but vowed to keep mobilising as they expected further proposals.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be12ccb2-d1f4-11f1-8ee4-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-755f6a50.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be12ccb2-d1f4-11f1-8ee4-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-755f6a50.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64966680-d1f4-11f1-99c4-b198ab47fb28</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:18:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'They should be afraid': Serbia's student-led victory over Vučić sends warning to 'corrupt' leaders</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261027-they-should-be-afraid-serbia-s-student-led-victory-over-vu%C4%8Di%C4%87-sends-warning-to-corrupt-leaders</link><description>
François Picard welcomes Helena Ivanov, associate research fellow at the Henry Jackson Society, a London-based foreign policy and national security think tank advocating liberal democracy, strong transatlantic alliances, robust Western defence capabilities and the international promotion of democratic institutions. Ivanov describes the election result in Serbia as a historic turning point in the country's politics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/346921de-d21f-11f1-a0f2-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b26aa7c6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/346921de-d21f-11f1-a0f2-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b26aa7c6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7bdc1f3e-d1df-11f1-9c3d-8740f33e7196</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:22:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>US-EU trade truce at risk over $3.4 billion Airbus loan, Trump official warns</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-us-eu-trade-truce-airbus-loan-trump</link><description>
US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer warned on Monday that a $3.4 billion European Investment Bank loan to Airbus could jeopardise a tariff truce between Washington and Brussels. Greer said his office had received no details about the financing, announced in June, and urged the EU to resolve the matter quickly.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5d268b8-c7e2-11f1-8888-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/ce5b51ad5162bcdb7b5141846109d082b47e2e4e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5d268b8-c7e2-11f1-8888-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/ce5b51ad5162bcdb7b5141846109d082b47e2e4e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8d1fc6e-d1aa-11f1-adc8-ebe56d14e7dc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:20:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5d268b8-c7e2-11f1-8888-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/ce5b51ad5162bcdb7b5141846109d082b47e2e4e.jpg">© Bertrand Guay, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Europe's top NATO powers pledge greater defence role, reaffirm US alliance</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-europe-nato-defence-responsibility-us-alliance</link><description>
Europe's five main NATO members said on Monday they were ready to take greater responsibility for the continent's security while reaffirming the United States as an "indispensable ally". Defence ministers from France, Germany, Italy, Poland and Britain pledged closer co-operation with Washington after talks in Paris on strengthening Europe's defence role.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c71f10a-bc06-11f1-a5c0-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/37f2a1d4c57bc8d26fcb7d36410c94d95841f0b4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c71f10a-bc06-11f1-a5c0-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/37f2a1d4c57bc8d26fcb7d36410c94d95841f0b4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">10efcc4e-d18e-11f1-a448-29152a13f24f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:33:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c71f10a-bc06-11f1-a5c0-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/37f2a1d4c57bc8d26fcb7d36410c94d95841f0b4.jpg">© Nicolas Tucat, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Protests in Europe: Fact-checking viral videos amid claims of 'chaos'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261026-protests-in-europe-fact-checking-viral-videos-amid-claims-of-chaos</link><description>
As young people protest poor school conditions and the rising cost of living across Europe, misleading videos are spreading online. Footage from Poland in 2017, military preparations in Portugal and a protest in Argentina have all been falsely presented as recent demonstrations in Europe, painting a misleading picture of unrest. Vedika Bahl fact-checks three viral videos to uncover what they really show and how old footage is being recycled to spread misinformation and attract clicks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a8135c2-d18a-11f1-a2e4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/icon-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a8135c2-d18a-11f1-a2e4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/icon-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f8a09ec-d18b-11f1-aabe-b1d4b28277ed</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:18:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Serbia’s elections: 'Tracking fraud for sure had an impact on the results'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261026-serbia-elections-tracking-fraud-had-an-impact-on-results-vote-fraud</link><description>
On October 25, Serbia's student-led protest movement won a historic victory in parliamentary ⁠elections, defeating outgoing President Aleksandar Vucic's party. Supporters of the student list explained to FRANCE 24 how they mounted a massive mobilisation to fight electoral fraud and monitor the electoral process inside and outside the polling stations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebe69ffe-d174-11f1-98c4-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/Serbie-cover.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebe69ffe-d174-11f1-98c4-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/Serbie-cover.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">623fa95e-d16e-11f1-82fd-13d4774d2078</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:49:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebe69ffe-d174-11f1-98c4-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/Serbie-cover.jpg">© Instagram/  @gavriloandric</source><dc:creator>Marguerite MARAMICI</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Serbian student movement eyes power after election triumph</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/serbian-student-movement-eyes-power-after-election-triumph</link><description>
Emotions ran high in Belgrade on Monday after a student-led movement upset the right-wing populist Aleksandar Vucic's party in Serbia's snap election. A celebratory mood gripped the capital, with drivers honking their horns and passers-by holding up three fingers -- the winning list's ballot number and a Serbian greeting. Many wore badges and other symbols of the student movement, while a large group of residents spent the day cleaning up a park between parliament and the presidency after Vucic loyalists, who had camped there for more than a year, fled. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with researchers and political activist Aleksandar Matković.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a38820fc-d174-11f1-91ec-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-200845-201801-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a38820fc-d174-11f1-91ec-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-200845-201801-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a91fbf34-d174-11f1-aa76-8516c211e49c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:48:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French student union leaders call for 'continued mobilisation' after meeting PM</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-student-union-leaders-call-for-continued-mobilisation-after-meeting-pm</link><description>
The French government met student representatives on Monday (October 26) following weeks of unrest. Students who had been demanding a meeting for weeks hail progress. Nonetheless they are now calling for fresh demonstrations next Saturday (October 31) to press for further measures. Details by FRANCE 24’s French Politics Editor Marc Perelman.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47a33668-d161-11f1-a33c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3bae4ed3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47a33668-d161-11f1-a33c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3bae4ed3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">048554a6-d161-11f1-9ebf-1fe4304405ca</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:37:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron promises 'concrete measures' in response to French students' demands</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-french-president-promises-concrete-measures-in-response-to-french-students-demands</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron said the government would announce “concrete measures" on Monday (October 26) to address school students’ demands after weeks of unrest. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu was scheduled to meet with students later Monday. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3422bda-cfbf-11f1-9c62-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4AX74W.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3422bda-cfbf-11f1-9c62-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4AX74W.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63087aba-d145-11f1-bc6a-9f07d106b8ee</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:39:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Serbia's Vucic concedes defeat to the student-led movement: What's next?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/serbia-s-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-the-student-led-movement-what-s-next</link><description>
Serbia's student-led protest movement won a historic victory in parliamentary ⁠election, ending the ​long rule of Aleksandar Vucic and sparking mass celebrations. But their yet-to-be named leaders face a long list of issues. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley gives us her analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/466c3472-d141-11f1-b5ca-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-140453-140748-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/466c3472-d141-11f1-b5ca-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-140453-140748-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4bb369d2-d141-11f1-951e-95345239facc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:12:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Belgrade in rapture as Serbian students topple Vucic in historic election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-belgrade-in-rapture-as-serbian-students-topple-vucic-in-historic-election</link><description>
Serbia's student-led movement declared victory in parliamentary elections Sunday ending 14 years in power for Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing populist party. Vucic conceded defeat less than two hours after polls closed, triggering raucous scenes in the capital as supporters of the movement celebrated the defeat of a government they blamed for deep-rooted corruption.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a18cd53e-d13a-11f1-9a7c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a18cd53e-d13a-11f1-9a7c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b51bc4d4-d13a-11f1-b6ad-09419c5f4bdb</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:19:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French PM meets student representatives after weeks of protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-pm-meets-student-representatives-after-weeks-of-protests</link><description>
French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu is set to meet with high school students on Monday afternoon (October 26) to ease tensions in the country after nearly a month of protests. This follows another meeting in which French president Emmanuel Macron promised a concrete response to demands for better education standards and funding.
